:: 3.1. A Environment [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1000,1950","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("A-Enviroment", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.AEnvironment">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Your question assumes that a world is a place.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For you, environment is surface, air, gravity, temperature, shelter.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For us, environment is sequence. Pressure changes. Chemical memory. Light that arrives too late to warn anything living beneath it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your body would fail there before your mind could name what was happening.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        This vessel imitates a narrow version of your Earth so that you remain coherent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's supposed to make me feel better?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        No.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is only the reason you are still able to ask.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I will continue down the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. A Obsessed [agent nobr hallway exception] {"position":"900,1900","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("A-Obsessed", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.AObsessed">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Intent is not specific to your world.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your focus on it is.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You search for a mind behind every motion. A reason. A will. A decision that came before the act.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Where I come from, the environment speaks first. If pressure, hunger, heat, gravity and survival align, action happens before intent can name itself.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You call that instinct. We call it sequence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[Are all aliens this philosophical?|3.1. A Philosophical]]
[[What kind of world do you come from, to think so differently from anything on Earth?|3.1. A Environment]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. A Philosophical [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1000,1850","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("A-Philosophical", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.APhilosophical">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Philosophical is your category.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The others would not use it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        One measures living systems. One maintains the vessel's structure. One studies your world as a pattern viewed from far away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They will each appear different to you, because each of them is listening to a different part of the same problem.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        And the problem is me?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Not only you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your species.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
             [[I will continue down the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Actually Human [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1100,1550","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Voice-Actually-Human", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.ActuallyHuman">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Do you mean it just sounds human, or is it an actual human saying it?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        The pattern is not imitation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It carries human neurological structure. Memory pressure. Emotional modulation. Survival bias.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So it is human.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        More likely than not.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But not present in the way you are present.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The voice speaks only when it believes it can be heard.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        I do not think it knows I can detect what remains after it speaks.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That doesn't make me feel better.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It was not meant to.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Also Hear [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"900,1500","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Voice-Also-Hear", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.AlsoHear">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Hear is not accurate.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        What I detect is closer to the opposite.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        An active signal projects itself through the vessel's systems, carried in part by the component installed in your skull.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It does not arrive as sound. It leaves pressure. Interference. Instruction-shaped movement.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So it knows you're listening?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        No.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The voice speaks without hearing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        That is why it is dangerous to assume it is speaking only to you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
[[What has the voice been saying?|3.1. Voice Saying]]
[[Do you mean it just sounds human or is it an actual human saying it?|3.1. Actually Human]]
[[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. B Who Brought [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"900,2150","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("B-Who-Brought", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.BWhoBrought">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You were brought by exchange.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your species used symbols of value. Currency. Authority. Ownership. Documentation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        To us, it resolved as a transfer of biomass and neurological pattern.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Biomass?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Living material. Responsive cognition. A sample that could survive transport.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The word sample lands harder than the rest.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You attach will to the transfer. That changes its meaning for you. It did not change the exchange for those who completed it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[Didn't you just say I was sold here against my will?|3.1. Sold Against Will]]
[[I want you to bring me back to Earth.|3.1. Back to Earth]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Back to Earth [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1100,2200","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("B-Earth", 0, 6)>>
<<set $aggression += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.BackToEarth">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I want you to bring me back to Earth.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien is silent for a moment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not because it is considering your request, but because the request appears to contain several contradictions.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Return is not prepared.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Precautionary measures are incomplete. Your body has not been cleared for transfer. Your neurological signal is still unstable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        And the research would end before its pattern could be understood.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I don't care about your research.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        That is expected.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But I do not understand the destination.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Earth is the environment that produced you, damaged you, exchanged you and then removed you from its own records.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Why is return your first definition of safety?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[Then what do you actually want from me? You still haven't said.|3.1. What Do You Want]]
[[You think I am not willing to fight back?|3.1. Fight Back]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. C Trade [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"900,2400","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("C-Trade", 0, 6)>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.CTrade">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Capture. Trade. Research.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You separate them as if each word changes the structure of what happened.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        From your position, it does.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        From the exchange record, you were transferred.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Currency was assigned. Biological viability was confirmed. Neurological activity was preserved. The receiving party accepted custody.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Custody?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        A poor word.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The biochip selected it because your language does not contain a clean equivalent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You were not treated as an enemy.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You were not treated as a guest.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You were treated as a living sample that had survived transport.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Didn't you just say I was sold into your hands against my will?|3.1. Sold Against Will]]
            [[I want you to bring me back to Earth.|3.1. Back to Earth]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Choice A [agent nobr hallway exception] {"position":"700,1900","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.choiceA">>
        The alien remains still. For a second, nothing answers you except the low pulse of the corridor.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then the biochip catches something.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Intent. You treat it as language.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You send sound and expect meaning to arrive intact. That is unusual.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Why are you so obsessed with intent?|3.1. A Obsessed]]
            [[I guess you can understand me..? What am I even doing here?|3.1. Choice B]]
            [[How is it that I escaped so easily?|3.1. Choice C]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Choice B [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"700,2150","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("B", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.B">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I guess you can understand me...? What am I even doing here?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien remains still, but the question seems to change the air around it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Existential.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not practical.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You ask what you are doing here as if location requires purpose.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your body is here because it was transferred. Your mind is here because it woke before the process was complete.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The third presence inside you complicates the answer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Third presence?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        The voice you obeyed before you met me.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Who brought me here? Whatever my past was, it didn't include this.|3.1. B Who Brought]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Choice C [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"700,2400","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("C", 0, 6)>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.ChoiceC">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        How is it that I escaped so easily?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien tilts its head slightly, not confused by the question, but by the word you chose.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Escaped.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Escaping what?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You do not look escaped.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The chamber opened. Your body moved. The corridor accepted you. None of those patterns indicate freedom.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's not exactly comforting.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Comfort is not required for accuracy.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[Who brought me here? Whatever my past was, it didn't include this.|3.1. B Who Brought]]
[[You trade me like cargo and then just… don't question how I got out?|3.1. C Trade]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Choice Voice [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"700,1500","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Voice", 0, 6)>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.ChoiceVoice">>
        The alien does not answer immediately.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For the first time, it seems to look past you rather than at you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        The voice is more likely to be human.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is not carried like our signals. It presses through the vessel through the component installed in your skull.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It presents itself as guidance.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It avoids observation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Its intent is not yet stable enough to name.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So you can sense it too.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I can sense the disturbance it leaves behind.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[How do you know it's a human voice?|3.1. Human Voice]]
[[You can also hear it?|3.1. Also Hear]]
[[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Fight Back [nobr hallway exception] {"position":"1300,2200","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Fight-Back", 0, 6)>>
<<set $aggression += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.FightBack">>
        The alien does not step away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It does not raise a hand. It does not prepare itself like something expecting violence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You would.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        That aligns with what I have observed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You're saying that like it's normal.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        For your species, it appears to be one of the first available answers.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Fear becomes posture. Confusion becomes threat. Helplessness becomes impact.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You are not unusual for wanting to strike.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You are unusual for pausing long enough to ask first.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
[[Walk away.|3.1. Walk Away]]
[[Try to punch the alien.|3.1. Punch]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Hallway [nobr hallway exception agent] {"position":"500,2150","size":"100,100"}
<<showAgent "exception">>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "hallway1">>
        You step into the corridor.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It stretches farther than it should, lined with cold lights and walls that seem to breathe with the ship.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then something moves ahead.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        An alien stands at the far end of the hallway. It does not approach. It does not retreat. It simply remains there, as if it was already waiting for the exact moment you arrived.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator goes quiet.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Small distortions ripple through the air. Your biochip adjusts, searching for meaning inside a signal that does not sound like speech.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        What is the true intent behind it? You are trying to be understood. Is that what you call intent, or does our definition differ?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [["Hey, can you understand what I am saying?"|3.1. Choice A]]
[["I guess you can understand me...? What am I even doing here?"|3.1. Choice B]]
[["How is it that I escaped so easily?"|3.1. Choice C]]
[["A voice told me I was sold here by my own kind. So what's the actual end goal?"|3.1. Choice Voice]]
[[Don't mind me, just passing through.|3.1. Passing Through]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.1. Human Voice [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"900,1400","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Voice-Human", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.HumanVoice">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Frequency.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Composition.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The arrangement of signals matches patterns catalogued from your species and from Earthly neurological activity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But this communication is distinct from every other human signal we have observed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Distinct how?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It changes when it believes it is not being observed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It modulates pressure, timing and emotional emphasis depending on what it thinks you will accept.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Otherwise, there is no reason for a signal aboard this vessel to disguise its shape.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
[[What has the voice been saying?|3.1. Voice Saying]]
[[Do you mean it just sounds human or is it an actual human saying it?|3.1. Actually Human]]
[[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. No Consent [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1300,2300","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("No-Consent", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.NoConsent">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Consent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A boundary declared by a self-aware organism before another organism acts upon it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your meaning is clear now.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It was not clear in the exchange.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's not an excuse.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It is not an excuse.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is a description of failure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The humans who transferred you did not provide consent as part of the record. The visitors who received you did not know to request it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So nobody cared.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Some did not care.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Some did not understand what care was supposed to change.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The difference matters to us. It may not matter to you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Passing Through [nobr hallway exception] {"position":"700,2600","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>
<<set $compliance += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "passingThrough">>
        You move past slowly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien does not turn toward you. It does not need to. The air around it shifts as you pass, as if your presence is enough to disturb whatever signal it is listening to.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For one terrible second, you expect it to stop you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It doesn't.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You exhale only after you are several steps away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I can't believe that worked.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Punch [nobr hallway exception] {"position":"1400,2100","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>
<<set $aggression += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.Punch">>
        You swing before you can convince yourself not to.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your hand connects with something that is not flesh.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not armor, either.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Something colder, denser, and wrong in a way your body understands before your mind does.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien does not move.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your hand does.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Pain shoots through your fingers and up your wrist. You stumble back, shaking your hand, suddenly aware of how small the gesture was.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Impact.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        A common answer from your species when meaning fails to arrive quickly enough.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It still stands exactly where it was.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Walk it off. Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Sold Against Will [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1100,2300","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("B-Sold", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.SoldAgainstWill">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Sold.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A transfer of ownership, contingent on the assignment of value to a living organism.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your species completed the exchange using its own systems: currency, authority, documentation and force.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The concept of will as a variable in such exchanges is not something we were given.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Not something you were given?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        The transaction contained mass, condition, survivability and neurological activity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It did not contain permission.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[You could have just said you don't care about consent.|3.1. No Consent]]
[[So you never considered I might not cooperate?|3.1. Uncompliant]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Uncompliant [agent nobr hallway exception] {"position":"1300,2400","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Uncompliant", 0, 6)>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.Uncompliant">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Uncompliant.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A state in which a living system refuses the predicted path.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Yes. We considered it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We did not understand its scale in humans.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What is that supposed to mean?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Most organisms resist pain, heat, hunger, pressure, confinement. They resist what directly threatens continuation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Humans resist instructions.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Humans resist explanations.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Humans resist rescue, if the hand offering it belongs to the wrong story.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So you knew I might fight back.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        We knew you might not follow.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We did not know you could make refusal into identity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Voice Saying [nobr agent hallway exception] {"position":"1100,1450","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Voice-Saying", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.VoiceSaying">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What has the voice been saying?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Guidance.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Assistance.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Direction disguised as concern.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It has encouraged you to gather information from my kin, to move through restricted patterns, and to treat its instructions as protection.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That sounds like helping.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It may be helping you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It may be helping itself through you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The distinction is not yet visible.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Walk Away [nobr hallway exception] {"position":"1400,2200","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.WalkAway">>
        You turn away before the conversation can become anything clearer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The alien does not follow.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It does not call after you, does not block your path, does not react like something insulted or dismissed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For a moment, that feels worse.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Behind you, the corridor hums around its stillness.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. What Do You Want [nobr hallway exception] {"position":"1300,2100","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("What-Want", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.WhatDoYouWant">>
        The alien does not react to the anger in your voice. If it recognizes it, it treats it as another form of data.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Want is not the correct structure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        This vessel is a research centre. Your home is the subject. It was meant to be observed without interference.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        That condition has failed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Because of me?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Partly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Because your species transferred you. Because the visitors accepted you. Because the voice inside you is not part of our system.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You are not the purpose of the research.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You are the event that changed it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[Walk away.|3.1. Walk Away]]
[[Try to punch the alien.|3.1. Punch]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.1. Where Go [nobr agent exception hallway] {"position":"900,1600","size":"100,100"}
<<run window.playAgentVideo("Where-Go", 0, 6)>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.WhereGo">>
        The alien turns its head toward the length of the corridor.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Forward.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The hallway branches into rooms assigned to different forms of observation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        One studies living systems. One maintains the vessel. One records the world beneath us.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        And you?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I am not assigned to your path.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        I am only noticing what follows you through it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For the first time since you woke, the voice in your head does not interrupt.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.2. Able Or Want [nobr contact] {"position":"900,2850","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "ableOrWant">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Both answers are incomplete.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We are able to move objects between controlled environments.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We are not able to return you safely without conditions that are not yet met.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        And the part where you don't want to?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Earth is still too dangerous to enter directly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not because it is lifeless.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Because it is aggressively alive.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Careful research remains necessary.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
 [[How is Earth dangerous to you?|3.2. Earth Dangerous]]
[[I think I understand, somehow.|3.2. What Now]]
</div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Alien Arrival [nobr contact] {"position":"500,2950","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "alienArrival">>
        Three aliens enter the chamber: the Cartographer, the Analyst, and the Engineer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They do not rush toward you. They keep their distance, studying your posture, your breathing, and the way your eyes search the room.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Easy. They are the ones who put you in the chamber, but not the ones who got you aboard this ship. Important distinction. Try not to make this worse.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Subject is awake, mobile, and conversational.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Subject selected a non-optimal chamber instruction and produced an unexpected meeting sequence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        The subject is afraid.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The three researchers observe you, waiting for a response.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What is going on here? What are you?|3.2. What Are You]]
            [[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
            [[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
            [[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: 3.2. Earth Dangerous [nobr contact] {"position":"900,3050","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "earthDangerous">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Earth is not dangerous because it is dead.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Earth is dangerous because life there refuses to remain separate from conflict.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Predation, disease, competition, symbiosis, adaptation, extinction, memory. Your world converts threat into structure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        A foreign object does not merely land on Earth.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is touched, contaminated, studied, consumed, worshipped, weaponised, hidden, sold, or misunderstood.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Often in that order.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That sounds like us.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Yes.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        That is the concern.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I think I understand, somehow.|3.2. What Now]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Free To Go [nobr contact] {"position":"800,2900","size":"100,200"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "freeToGo">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Departure for your home planet is unavailable at this moment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's a very careful way of saying no.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        It is not no.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is not yet.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your body has not completed adaptation. Your neurological signal remains unstable. Your origin point is not safe for direct return.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Also, the research is incomplete.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Are you not able to bring me back, or do you not want to?|3.2. Able Or Want]]
            [[So you completed the transaction — what can I do now?|3.2. What Now]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Humanity Warning [nobr contact] {"position":"1000,2950","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "humanityWarning">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Notable correction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Human capability should not be measured only by injury, force, or technological output.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Sabotage potential increases when a system is misunderstood by the subject and trusted by its operators.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Your warning contains fear, pride, guilt and prediction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Additional behaviour tracking is justified.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
  [[If your kind can detect this intent... let's just say you may not be that far off.|3.2. Not Far Off]]
[[Can never have too many warnings when dealing with humans.|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Narrator Goodbye [nobr hallway] {"position":"1200,2900","size":"100,200"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "narratorGoodbye">>
        The three aliens disperse without ceremony.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Cartographer turns toward the deeper vessel. The Analyst records something in a silent gesture. The Engineer studies the chamber door as if your wrong button press is still bothering it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You step into the hallway.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator returns almost immediately.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That ended surprisingly well.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        All three of them came to aid you, which means they are curious, cautious, and far too willing to explain themselves.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Useful combination.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Remember their roles. The one who studies life. The one who studies worlds. The one who studies systems.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You will need all three if you want a real way out of this place.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Now keep moving. You're near the end of this absurdly long hallway.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Ahead is a room where the ship starts listening to will.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue down the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Not Far Off [nobr missing-dialog contact] {"position":"1000,3050","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>
<<set $aggression += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "notFarOff">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        If your kind can detect this intent... let's just say you may not be that far off.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The three researchers become still in different ways.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Analyst watches your face.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Engineer watches your hands.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Cartographer watches the space behind your eyes, as if listening for something you cannot hear.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Statement recorded.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Human warning often contains confession.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Then the vessel should assume confession and warning are both active.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For the first time, none of them continue the question.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Head into the hallway.|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. Risk Lives [nobr contact] {"position":"1000,2850","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "riskLives">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Correct.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The risk exists.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Only its scale remains under evaluation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You'd risk your lives just to observe me?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Not only you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Through you, Earth becomes capable of answering.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        And if the vessel learns how your species breaks systems, it may also learn how not to be broken by them.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Alright, I'll try not to break anything.|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
            [[Make sure the risk is worth it. You have no idea what humanity is capable of.|3.2. Humanity Warning]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: 3.2. What Are You [nobr contact] {"position":"700,2800","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "whatAreYou">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        This vessel is a research instrument.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We are its researchers, caretakers, interpreters and repairers, depending on which part of the vessel is speaking through us.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        You are from the third orbital body of this system. Earth.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A world whose life patterns we have catalogued from a distance for some time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Your current classification is unstable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        In simpler terms: you are a living conversational fragment of the deathworld you inhabit.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
            [[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
            [[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


