:: Awakening Chamber [nobr waking] {"position":"200,2550","size":"100,100"}
<<audio ":all" stop>>
<<audio "awakening" loop play>>
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "awakeningChamber">>
        Water drains from somewhere above your head.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For a moment, there is no floor, no ceiling, no memory. Only glass, pressure, and the sound of your own breathing inside your skull.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Okay. You're awake. That's the hard part done, for both of us, honestly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You're not on Earth. I know that's a lot to absorb in the first five seconds. Take a breath. The environment is stable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Two illuminated controls pulse on the inside of the chamber.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        There are two buttons in front of you. Hit the right one. It opens the exit seal.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        The left one runs a pressure check you don't need. Trust me, this is not the time to become curious about alien safety procedures.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The right control reads: EXIT.  
        The left control reads: ENTER.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
        [[Press the right button — EXIT.|Right Button]]
        [[Press the left button — ENTER.|Left Button]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Activation [nobr core burn] {"position":"3200,5550","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnActivation">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not a command. The word a person uses when they are out of arguments and down to bare wire.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know what you're going to do. I know I can't stop you. I want to say something before you do it. Not to change your mind. Just. I need you to hear something.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Say it.|Burn Say It]]
            [[No.|Burn No]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Activation [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3200,5150","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionActivation">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        His voice cuts in for the first time since you entered this section.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know what you're going to do. I know I can't stop you. I want to say something before you do it. Not to change your mind. Just. I need you to hear something."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Say it.|Burn Exception Say It]]
            [[No.|Burn Exception Panel]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Led [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3000,5100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionLed">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You led me here on purpose.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I provided information. What you did with it was your own.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's not an answer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        No. I led you here on purpose. You asked for an answer so there it is. I observed the first person and I did not intervene and they died and I have been holding that as a variable without a function for a long time. You are not them. But you are the same kind of thing. I wanted to see if the outcome could be different.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Is it?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You are standing in the Fusion Core. You are alive. You are making a choice. That is already different.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What do you want me to do?|Burn Exception What]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
            [[Walk away.|Burn Exception Walk]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Narrator [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3000,5000","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionNarrator">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        In the control room. He cannot reach this part of the ship. The frequency he uses to keep the others out also keeps him in. I wondered how long it would take him to notice that. It has been longer than I expected.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You came.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[You led me here on purpose.|Burn Exception Led]]
            [[What do you want me to do?|Burn Exception What]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Panel [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3600,5100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionPanel">>
        You press the panel. A low tone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Is that— is it in there with you?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A pause.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Of course it is. I spent months watching it drift through this ship like it had nowhere to be. I thought it was nothing. Just an extra. I thought I was the interesting one.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A long beat. Then, very quietly:
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Well played. I mean that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Burn Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Say It [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3400,5100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionSayIt">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have spent a long time believing that humanity is worth something. Not in the abstract — I mean specifically worth it. I believed that if I could just get out of this room and get this ship moving then something would change. For the argument. For the idea that we deserve to be part of whatever this is. And maybe I was wrong. Maybe the thing I was trying to prove is exactly what I disproved by trying to prove it. I love this species. I love it completely. Even right now. Even this.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Press the panel.|Burn Exception Panel]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception Walk [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3200,5050","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionWhat">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Then walk away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It steps aside. No further comment. You arrive at the control room. The narrator is surprised — you took the long way around. He finds this, unexpectedly, moving.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending A Curiosity]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Exception What [nobr core burn exception] {"position":"3000,5200","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionWhat">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I want nothing. Want implies an absence I'm trying to fill. I told you that. But I will tell you what I observe. The voice in your head has been in that room for a long time. Long enough to stop being a person in some ways that matter. Long enough to stop being able to see the difference between using someone and helping them. The ship holds data that has taken decades to gather. The voice needs you to leave this room and walk to the control room and place your hand on a panel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Beat.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        There is also a panel here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
            [[Walk away.|Burn Exception Walk]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Final [nobr core burn] {"position":"3800,5300","size":"100,100"}
<<audio ":all" stop>>
<<audio "burnEnding" loop play>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnFinal">>
        The four-minute countdown is not displayed as a number. It is felt. The heat changes. The hum shifts register. The lights don't flicker — they clarify, briefly, as the systems maximise before they fail.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I have been observing for a very long time. I have observed birth and continuation and the end of both. I have never observed something choose. Not like this. Not with full information and no survival pressure and the ability to walk away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A pause. Something in its register that is as close to warmth as it gets.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Your species is genuinely the strangest thing in this system. I will not be able to tell anyone that. But I know it now. That seems like enough.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship ends. The research ends. The narrator ends. The Exception ends, with its particular form of patience. You end — not because of the biochip this time, but because you chose a thing larger than the biochip.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Blackout.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship was observed to descend from its orbital position at 03:14 UTC.
        No distress signal was recorded.
        No wreckage was recovered.
        The research consortium filed a report attributing the loss to navigational failure.
        The Exception's absence from the vessel was not noted in the report.
        It had not been listed as a research subject.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Narrator Body [nobr core burn narrator] {"position":"3000,5500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNarratorBody">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Because something prevented it. The ship's systems don't refuse. They don't make exceptions. Something would have had to actively—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He stops. His voice, for the first time, has no cadence to it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Something kept that body there. Something wanted you to find it. Something wanted you to have a reason to…
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He looks at the controls behind you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have been in this room because the frequency keeps the aliens out. I told you that. I did not tell you I could also not leave. The frequency works in both directions. I have been in this room for a very long time. And something has been watching me be in it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[You were used too.|Burn Narrator Used]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Activation]]
            [[Walk away with me.|Burn Walk Away]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Narrator Knew [nobr core burn narrator] {"position":"3000,5400","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNarratorKnew">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I knew they died. I did not know the body was still there. I want that distinction to mean something and I understand if it doesn't.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Why did the ship not process the body?|Burn Narrator Body]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Activation]]
            [[Walk away with me.|Burn Walk Away]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Narrator Used [nobr core burn narrator] {"position":"3000,5600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNarratorUsed">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. I think so. I think I have been someone else's instrument for longer than I was my own plan. And I thought I was so careful. I thought I knew how people worked. It turns out knowing the shape of something and knowing what it will do are not the same. I should have known that. That's one of the things I used to say.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Activation]]
            [[Walk away with me.|Burn Walk Away]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn No [nobr core burn] {"position":"3400,5550","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNo">>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Press the panel.|Burn Panel Narrator]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Panel Narrator [nobr core burn narrator] {"position":"3600,5500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnPanelNarrator">>
        The control panel. A single large interface. The biochip translates it without being asked: EMERGENCY SHUTDOWN. IRREVERSIBLE. You press it. A low tone. Not dramatic. Just a sound that means something has begun that cannot be undone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I've been in this room alone for a long time. Having company at the end is…
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He doesn't finish the sentence. He has chosen to stay, though he hasn't said it and won't say it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Burn Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Say It [nobr core burn] {"position":"3400,5450","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnSayIt">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have spent a long time believing that humanity is worth something. Not in the abstract — I mean specifically worth it, worth the effort of everything I did to get here and everything it cost and everyone it cost. I believed that if I could just get out of this room and get this ship moving then something would change. For the argument. For the idea that we deserve to be part of whatever this is. And maybe I was wrong. Maybe the thing I was trying to prove is exactly what I disproved by trying to prove it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Something in him gives way.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I think you might be the most human thing that has happened on this ship. And I think that's going to be true whether you press that or not. I love this species. I love it completely. Even right now. Even this.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Press the panel.|Burn Panel Narrator]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Burn Walk Away [nobr core burn] {"position":"3200,5450","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnWalkAway">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright. Yes. Yes, let's try that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You leave the Fusion Core. You arrive at the control room. He is surprised — you took the long way around. He finds this, unexpectedly, moving.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending A Curiosity]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: CR Believe [nobr narrator agent missing-features] {"position":"5300,2900","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "CRBelieve">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That is the question I have been not asking myself for a very long time. I believe in humanity the way some people believe in a god. Not because I have proof. Because the alternative — not believing in it — requires me to look at everything I've done and find a different explanation for why I did it. And I don't have one. So I keep believing. I believe harder when I'm least sure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You asked if it's something I say. It started as something I believed. Then it became something I said because I believed it. Then it became something I said to keep believing it. I'm not sure which one it is right now, standing here, looking at you. I think that's the most honest thing I've said since you walked through that door.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Who are you really?|CR Who Are You]]
			[[What exactly do you need from me?|CR What Need]]
			[[You used me. You used the other person too and they died.|CR Used Me]]
			[[You've been watching me this whole time through the biochip.|CR Biochip Watch]]
			[[The body in that room. You said the ship processes everything. It didn't process them.|CR Body Question]]
			[[Your organisation. Who do they actually answer to?|CR Organisation]]
			[[Did you grieve them? The first person.|CR Grieve]]
            [[Continue.|CR Panel Speech]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: CR Biochip Watch [nobr agent narrator missing-features] {"position":"5300,2500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "CRBiochipWatch">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. Everything you said to them. Everything you did. The layout of every room. I had reasons for needing to know. I told myself the reasons were good enough. I'm less certain of that now than I was when I started.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[So everything I said to the aliens, you heard.|CR Heard Everything]]
            [[Did you ever intervene in what I said to them?|CR Intervene]]
            [[Who are you really?|CR Who Are You]]
			[[What exactly do you need from me?|CR What Need]]
			[[You used me. You used the other person too and they died.|CR Used Me]]
			[[The body in that room. You said the ship processes everything. It didn't process them.|CR Body Question]]
			[[Your organisation. Who do they actually answer to?|CR Organisation]]
			[[Did you grieve them? The first person.|CR Grieve]]
			[[Do you actually believe humanity is worth what you've done for it?|CR Believe]]
            [[Continue.|CR Panel Speech]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: CR Body Question [nobr agent narrator missing-features] {"position":"5300,2600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "CRBodyQuestions">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know. I've been thinking about that since you found it. The ship doesn't make exceptions. Something kept that body there. Something wanted you to find it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What would want that?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Something that knew you were coming before I did. Something that understood that you finding that room would change what you did next. I have been in this room for a long time and I thought I understood the shape of everything happening on this ship. I was wrong about that. I don't know by how much.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Who are you really?|CR Who Are You]]
			[[What exactly do you need from me?|CR What Need]]
			[[You used me. You used the other person too and they died.|CR Used Me]]
			[[You've been watching me this whole time through the biochip.|CR Biochip Watch]]
			[[Your organisation. Who do they actually answer to?|CR Organisation]]
			[[Did you grieve them? The first person.|CR Grieve]]
			[[Do you actually believe humanity is worth what you've done for it?|CR Believe]]
            [[Continue.|CR Panel Speech]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: CR Grieve [nobr agent narrator missing-features] {"position":"5300,2800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "CRGrieve">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I told myself what happened to them was a miscalculation. I use that word because it keeps it in a register I can manage. Grief is not a register I can manage in this room. I've been alone in here for long enough that I'm not sure I have access to it anymore in the way I used to. But I think about them. I think about them with a frequency that isn't consistent with just filing it as a miscalculation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[That's not an answer.|CR Grieve Not Answer]]
            [[I think you do.|CR Grieve Think You Do]]
			[[You used me. You used the other person too and they died.|CR Used Me]]
			[[You've been watching me this whole time through the biochip.|CR Biochip Watch]]
