:: Cart Punch [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3000,875","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartPunch">>
        You strike the Cartographer before the thought finishes becoming a decision.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your hand connects with its lower limb.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It is not flesh.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The surface fractures like mineral glass under pressure, releasing a thin yellow mist that curls close to the floor.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Step away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The vapour is not meant for you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes, good, excellent moment to discover alien self-defense chemistry. Move back.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You retreat, shaking pain out of your hand.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Cartographer remains upright. The fractured surface folds inward, slowly sealing itself.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Impact recorded.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The act produced pain in you, damage in me, and no additional understanding.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        That may be the understanding.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Fine. Can I join you in research?|Cart Join Research]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cart Puzzle Sacrifice [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3400,1025","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartPuzzleSacrifice">>
        The second projection appears.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A person carrying another through fire.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A body placed between danger and someone smaller.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Hands reaching back even when escape would be easier alone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        This pattern is irregular.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        An organism ending or risking its own continuation for another.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It contradicts direct survival logic.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You mean sacrifice.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Your word suggests value created by loss.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We can observe the loss.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The value remains difficult to map.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Of course it isn't passed on easily. Sacrifice ends with death.|Sacrifice Death]]
            [[There is no greater design — we just exist inside an existing framework.|Sacrifice No Design]]
            [[There are many interpretations. Most people attribute it to divine figures.|Sacrifice Divine]]
            [The self extends into what it loves. Survival relocates.|Sacrifice Consciousness]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cart Puzzle Science [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3400,775","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartPuzzleScience">>
        The third projection forms.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Laboratories. Equations. Launch towers. Microscopes. Reactors. Satellites. Tools built to look deeper than the body was ever meant to see.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        This pattern shows coherence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You attempt to understand your environment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The result is further disruption of that environment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's called progress.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Progress is your moral framing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The pattern itself is simpler.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You discover.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You apply.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You weaponize.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You regret.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then you discover again.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Isn't it natural that understanding leads to development which can be weaponised?|Science Weapons]]
            [[And your fundamentals are just sitting around not doing all that, I'm guessing?|Science Your Kind]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cart Puzzle War [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3400,525","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartPuzzleWar">>
        The first projection expands.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Armies. Borders. Smoke over cities. Flags raised over places that were already occupied by living people.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        This pattern is the most consistent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your species organizes itself around opposition with unusual regularity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        On many worlds, conflict decreases when scarcity decreases.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Yours does not.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You fight when lacking.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You fight when not lacking.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You fight over matter, memory, belief, territory, prediction, insult, inheritance and symbols.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        You call this war.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Conflict is not unusual.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Conflict becoming identity is unusual.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[There's no way you never knew conflicts until coming here. That's impossible.|War No Conflict]]
            [[What do you mean conflict isn't usually found between lifeforms?|War Between Lifeforms]]
            [[Did you find any parallels between us in how we socialise?|War Parallels]]
            [[War is a normal part of life. The more you dwell on it the more it consumes you.|War Normal]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cart Signal Check [nobr archive cartographer] {"position":"4000,775","size":"100,100"}
<<set $archiveSignal = true>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartSignalCheck">>
        The projection collapses into a thin line of light.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It does not enter your hand.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It enters the biochip.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For a second, you feel a shape rather than hear a word: Earth as pattern, Earth as contradiction, Earth as something dangerous because it is alive.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        There. That's one of the signals.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Archive signal acquired.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Your translator has retained the classification.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It will not be meaningful alone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        No, but it is useful, and useful is what we need right now.
    <<ctpNext clear>>

        <<if $specimenSignal and $engineeringSignal>>
            <<speaker "Narrator">>
            That's all three. Come back to the locked door.
        <<elseif $specimenSignal or $engineeringSignal>>
            <<speaker "Narrator">>
            Two signals down. One left.
        <<else>>
            <<speaker "Narrator">>
            One signal down. Two left.
        <</if>>

    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Return to the central room.|Pre Control Room]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cart Threatening [nobr agent cartographer] {"position":"2600,675","size":"100,100"}

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartThreaten">>
    	<<speaker "Cartographer">>
        The classification holds. An extreme lifeform by any framework we have applied. Threats are found everywhere in the universe, but no such lifeforms are threatening in the way they are on deathworlds. This one is a keen example.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[That's a lot of effort being spent on research.|Cart Effort]]
            [[I might have heard that deathworld thing before. Surely Earth isn't that dangerous?|Cart Deathworld]]
            [[So what is there to do? Can I join you in research?|Cart Join Research]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Cartographer Main [nobr agent archive cartographer] {"position":"2400,775","size":"100,100"}
<<showAgent "cartographer">>


<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "cartographerMain">>
    	<<speaker "Cartographer">>
        These are the vessel's recorded patterns, also known as the Archive. The vessel's means of observing the dense patterns observed from below.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What kind of patterns are you observing exactly?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Conflict. Cooperation. Collapse. Reconstruction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Your world cycles through them with unusual frequency.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        We have not determined if this is inefficiency or a greater design meant to threaten the wider scope.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I was under the impression your kind doesn't know what threatening means?|Cart Threatening]]
			[[That's a lot of effort being spent on research.|Cart Effort]]
			[[Surely Earth isn't that dangerous?|Cart Deathworld]]
			[[So what is there to do out here? Can I join you in any research?|Cart Join Research]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Code Entry [nobr control code] {"position":"4600,2550","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "codeEntry">>
        The locked door does not open when you approach.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Instead, a panel rises from the wall, forming three empty frequency channels.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The biochip reacts before you do.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Three signal patterns surface in your vision, not as numbers at first, but as pressure, rhythm, and shape.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your hand moves toward the panel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. That's it. Let the chip translate it. Don't overthink the part where your body knows what to do before you do.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The final line locks into place.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The door opens.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Good. Now come in. I have been waiting for quite a long time, and I am afraid my patience has become less of a virtue and more of a medical condition.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Enter the control room.|Control Room Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


