:: Control Room Entry [nobr control narrator] {"position":"4800,2550","size":"100,100"}
<<audio ":all" stop>>
<<audio "control" loop play>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "controlRoomEntry">>
        The control room is smaller than expected. Dense with repurposed alien interfaces half-dismantled and rebuilt with whatever was available. At the center: a single seat facing a wall of screens, most of them dark. Sitting in the seat is a man. Tall, or was. Broad-shouldered in a jacket that was probably fitted once. Reddish face. Reddish hair, or what remains of it. His suit was once a suit. Now it is a garment that has been slept in, worked in, and lived in for long enough that the original intention is visible only in the lapels, which are still crisp in the way that lapels sometimes stubbornly remain crisp when everything else has given up. He looks up. His eyes are very alert. That is the most unsettling part.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The biochip begins to malfunction. Visual distortions. Not painful. But disorienting.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. Yes, that's the room doing that. It's not dangerous. Well. Not immediately. The frequency is calibrated for their range, not yours, so you get a residual. It's unpleasant but it's manageable. I have managed it for quite some time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Welcome. Apologies for the… all of this."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Control Room Explanation]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Control Room Explanation [nobr control narrator] {"position":"4900,2550","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "controlRoomExplanation">>
        He stands too quickly, gestures at the panel to the left, sits back down.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        The panel. Over there. It reads your biochip. When it does that — when it reads you specifically, a person who's been through the ship, who the ship has logged — it registers an authorised presence instead of a research subject and I get navigational control. That's the whole thing. That's what all of this was for. The code, the signals, the long conversations with the aliens. Those were for you. To get you here in a state where you might actually walk across this room rather than immediately try to— well. No need to dwell on that now.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You're further along than I expected, for what it's worth.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Control Room Questions]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Control Room Questions [nobr missing-features control questions narrator] {"position":"5100,2550","size":"100,100"}
<<showAgent "narrator">>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "controlRoomQuestions">>
        He waits. You can speak before you decide anything.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You made it. I want to say I'm surprised but that would be dishonest and I think you've earned honesty at this point. You've been pulling at threads since the awakening chamber. I noticed. I noticed every time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You talked to all of them. Really talked to them. I've watched people come through this ship and treat those aliens like obstacles. You treated them like they had something worth hearing. I find that genuinely moving, which is not what I expected to feel right now.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Good. You followed it through. I know that probably sounds like a small thing but it isn't. You had every reason to stop and you didn't. Come in.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Still standing. Still moving. You've been angry since the chamber and it hasn't stopped you once. I respect that more than I probably should. Come in. Let's finish this.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You made it. Come in.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You questioned everything I said and then went and asked better questions of your own. I want you to know that I noticed that specifically. The aliens noticed it too, which is rarer than you'd think.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Who are you really?|CR Who Are You]]
			[[What exactly do you need from me?|CR What Need]]
			[[You used me. You used the other person too and they died.|CR Used Me]]
			[[You've been watching me this whole time through the biochip.|CR Biochip Watch]]
			[[The body in that room. You said the ship processes everything. It didn't process them.|CR Body Question]]
			[[Your organisation. Who do they actually answer to?|CR Organisation]]
			[[Did you grieve them? The first person.|CR Grieve]]
			[[Do you actually believe humanity is worth what you've done for it?|CR Believe]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Death A [nobr missing-features ending control gameover] {"position":"7000,1550","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "deathA">>
        The ship moves. The narrator navigates. The screens come alive. For a long moment it seems like it might be fine. Then the biochip, still malfunctioning from the control room's frequency, reaches a threshold it was not designed to survive. Not an explosion. Not a scream. Just a failure of the thing that was keeping your nervous system calibrated to the alien environment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        No. No no—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He is at the panel. He does something frantic and incorrect. Then something else. Then he stops. There is nothing to undo.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I should have— the exposure time. I knew about the exposure time. I thought— I kept thinking there would be more—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He sits down on the floor. Not in the chair. On the floor. Just sits there.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I'm sorry. That isn't enough but it's what I have.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        They knew. The whole time, they knew what I was doing. And they came through the door anyway. I don't—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He stops. There is nothing to finish with.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Exception, somewhere on the ship, becomes still. Not the stillness of waiting. A different kind.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It asked good questions. That is not nothing. That is, in fact, considerable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        They fought the whole way. Right to the end. I want to be able to say that was the problem. I don't think it was the problem.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator sits down on the floor. Not in the chair. On the floor. The screens are alive around him. He doesn't look at them for a long time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship was observed to depart its orbital position at 03:14 UTC.
        No distress signal was recorded.
        No wreckage was recovered.
        The research consortium filed a report attributing the loss to navigational failure.
        The Exception's absence from the vessel was not noted in the report.
        It had not been listed as a research subject.  
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Death C [nobr ending control gameover] {"position":"7000,2750","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "deathC">>
        You leave the control room. The biochip, no longer screened by the room's frequency emitter, attempts to recalibrate. It has been running degraded for too long. The hallway outside the control room is the last thing you see.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        For what it's worth… you were exactly what I thought you'd be. I mean that in the only way that matters.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Silence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It watched. Until the end. That is not nothing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship remained in orbit.
        The Narrator filed no report.
        The Exception was observed at the window of the archive bay for some time after.
        It did not move away from it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


