        They were frightened before I could finish explaining anything. The biochip reacted badly. Their brain reacted worse.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It moved faster than I anticipated.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You knew they died.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I knew they died.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        I did not know they were here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        That distinction matters.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        It matters to the voice.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Do not listen to that thing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        The voice prefers urgency when memory becomes specific.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Did you do this?|Discarded Did You]]
            [[Talk to Exception.|Discarded Exception]]
            [[I don't want to be in here.|Discarded Leave]]
            [[Return to the archive.|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Discarded Why Telling [nobr agent exception discarded] {"position":"3200,1525","size":"100,100"}
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "discardedWhyTelling">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Why are you telling me this?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Because the first one could not return from this point.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Return where?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        To uncertainty.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They moved from confusion to obedience too quickly. Then from obedience to panic.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The voice survived both transitions.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They did not.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        And you think I can do something different?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I do not know.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        I am telling you because not knowing has become more useful than silence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What are you suggesting I do?|Discarded What Suggest]]
            [[So the narrator has been lying.|Discarded Lying]]
            [[I will return to the archive.|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Ending A Aggression [nobr ending aggression] {"position":"6700,1250","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingACuriosity">>
        You place your hand on the panel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright. I expected you to make me work for that. I had arguments prepared. Contingencies. You didn't make me use any of them. I think that's more frightening than if you had. A person who's been angry this whole time and still chooses to help — I don't have a framework for that. The aliens don't either. I checked.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Don't tell anyone I said that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Ending A Choice [nobr missing-dialog missing-features ending] {"position":"6400,1550","size":"100,200"}
<<set _c to $curiosity / 34>>
<<set _s to $skepticism / 37>>
