:: Eng Camera [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3200,4225","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCamera">>
        A camera rises from the workbench.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        It captures light and stores it. The function is clear. The purpose is not. Explain.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Stores memories.|Eng Camera Memory]]
            [[Shares experiences.|Eng Camera Share]]
            [[Obsession replaces experience.|Eng Camera Obsession]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Accuracy [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,4075","size":"100,100"}
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraAccuracy">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        If accuracy is the purpose, then this device surpasses the organism. But your species builds this device and then selects which images to keep and which to discard — a filter based on meaning, not fidelity. Why retain only the meaningful? What happens to accuracy there?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Because we don't want to experience things alone.|Eng Camera Alone]]
            [[Because the moment leaves something behind that can't be kept any other way.|Eng Camera Residue]]
            [[Obsession replaces experience.|Eng Camera Obsession]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Alone [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,4175","size":"100,100"}
<<set $compliance += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraAlone">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Not alone. The opposite of solitude is proximity. But proximity without transfer produces nothing. Your species seeks the transfer itself, not merely the closeness. The image is proof that something was felt. A signal to another organism that says: I was here and it was real.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 88.3 — 7.1 — 22.9
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Exit the engineering bay.|Eng Bay Closing]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Imprecision [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,3975","size":"100,100"}
<<set $compliance += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraImprecision">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        The imprecision. That is the purpose. Not to capture what was but to carry something forward through the distortion. We have found no equivalent mechanism in organisms that do not die.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 88.3 — 7.1 — 22.9
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Exit the engineering bay.|Eng Bay Closing]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Memory [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3400,4025","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraMemory">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Stores. Memories are not stored by organisms — they are reconstructed, each time slightly differently. This device stores a fixed image. The organism stores a changing impression. Which is more accurate?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[The organism's. The imprecision is the point.|Eng Camera Imprecision]]
            [[The device is more accurate. Accuracy is what matters.|Eng Camera Accuracy]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Obsession [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3400,4425","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraObsession">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Obsession. A fixation that persists past the point of useful return. And you propose this replaces the original event entirely. The image becomes the experience. The record becomes the memory. This is inefficient.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[That's the point.|Eng Camera Obsession Point]]
            [[No, that's the problem.|Eng Camera Obsession Problem]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Obsession Point [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,4375","size":"100,100"}
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraObsessionPoint">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        The inefficiency is intentional. You replace the lived experience because the lived experience was insufficient. The image is what you wished the moment had been. This device does not capture what happened. It captures what you needed to happen. That is an extraordinary function for a mechanical object.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 88.3 — 7.1 — 22.9
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Exit the engineering bay.|Eng Bay Closing]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Obsession Problem [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,4475","size":"100,100"}
<<set $compliance += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraObsessionProblem">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        You identify it as a malfunction. And yet you continue to use the device anyway. The species recognises the problem and perpetuates it. This is either a failure of correction or evidence that the problem serves a function you have not yet named.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 88.3 — 7.1 — 22.9
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Exit the engineering bay.|Eng Bay Closing]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Residue [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3600,4275","size":"100,100"}
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraResidue">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        The residue of experience. You have described a form of preservation that operates outside of the organism's body. External memory. And yet what is preserved is not information but significance. This device captures neither. What the image holds is something your species added after the fact.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 88.3 — 7.1 — 22.9
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Exit the engineering bay.|Eng Bay Closing]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Eng Camera Share [nobr agent engineer] {"position":"3400,4225","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engCameraShare">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        Shares. You give another organism access to a moment they did not live. The image becomes a bridge. We do not share experiences. We observe them. The distinction appears significant to your species. Clarify why transfer matters when the original moment has already passed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Because we don't want to experience things alone.|Eng Camera Alone]]
            [[Because the moment leaves something behind that can't be kept any other way.|Eng Camera Residue]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


