:: Hallway Convergence [nobr hallway] {"position":"1800,2525","size":"100,200"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "hallwayConvergence">>
        The corridor stretches forward, colder and wider than the one behind you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For the first time since waking, both paths feel as if they have collapsed into the same direction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Good. You're moving. That is, historically, the part people struggle with.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        What you met back there — the researchers, the Exception, whatever version of this route you took — that's the shape of things on this ship. Strange is the baseline here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Ahead is the central room before the control door. From there, three branches. Each of them contains something you need.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Don't worry about understanding all of it yet. Just reach the room.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Reach the room before the control room.|Pre Control Room]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Arrival [nobr intro arrival] {"position":"0,2200","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introArrival">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Their arrival did not unite humanity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It gave every government, every army, every movement and every frightened citizen the same question.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        What do you do when something looks down at your entire species and refuses to explain itself?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For a while, people simply watched.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then watching became fear.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        And fear became organization.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Intro Riots]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Backstory [nobr intro backstory] {"position":"0,2300","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introBackstory">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        The year is 2137.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Long before you woke inside the vessel, Earth had already begun to fracture.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        At first, it looked like a communication failure. Lost satellites. Dead emergency channels. Government feeds marked classified before anyone could explain why.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then the world learned the signal was not broken.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Something was answering from above.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Intro Earth]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Earth [nobr intro earth] {"position":"100,2300","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introEarth">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        The first vessels appeared over Earth decades ago.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They did not attack. They did not land. They simply remained above the atmosphere, silent enough for every nation to imagine its own ending.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        For three days, humanity watched the sky.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        On the fourth, the world stopped pretending it was in control.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Intro Arrival]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Exchange [nobr intro exchange] {"position":"0,2100","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introExchange">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        In the new order, some people discovered that fear could be organized.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The visitors did not understand ownership the way humans did. They did not understand ransom, trafficking, betrayal or consent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        They understood samples. Patterns. Biological records from a violent world.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        So certain human groups gave them exactly that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Living specimens, wrapped in paperwork and lies.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Intro Kidnapping]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Kidnapping [nobr intro kidnapping] {"position":"100,2100","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introKidnapping">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You were not chosen.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You were listed.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Moved through hands that never needed your name, only your weight, your blood type and the confirmation that the implant could survive transport.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Somewhere above you, people negotiated.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Somewhere beside them, the visitors watched without understanding what had been taken.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        And somewhere inside your skull, the first signal was already waiting to wake.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Awakening Chamber]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


:: Intro Riots [nobr intro riots] {"position":"100,2200","size":"100,100"}
<<hideAgent>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "introRiots">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Governments fell quietly at first.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not all at once. Not in one grand collapse. A missed broadcast here. A military order ignored there. A city left without an answer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Then people stopped waiting for the systems to protect them.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Streets became borders. Movements became armies. Fear became currency.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        And in the spaces where governments used to stand, new powers learned how to sell anything.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue|Intro Exchange]]
        </div>
    <</ctp>>
</div>


