:: War Between Lifeforms [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3600,525","size":"100,100"}
<<set $curiosity += 1>>
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warBetweenLifeforms">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Conflict exists.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But on many worlds it remains local, temporary, or environmental.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Hunger. Space. Reproduction. Temperature. Immediate survival.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        On Earth, conflict survives after the original pressure ends.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your species remembers injury as structure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You inherit borders drawn by people no longer alive.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You continue arguments started before your birth.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You create symbols, then suffer for them as if they were weather.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That's a very alien way of saying we have history.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        History appears to be conflict with storage.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I guess there's not many differences then, surprisingly.|War No Difference]]
            [[Did you find any parallels between your kind and mine?|War Parallels]]
            [[War is a normal part of life.|War Normal]]
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: War No Conflict [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3600,425","size":"100,100"}
<<set $skepticism += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warNoConflict">>
        [ BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 119.5 — 1.2 — 45.1 ]
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        We know friction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We know imbalance, correction, pressure, failure and environmental opposition.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We did not know conflict as identity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That sounds like a technical dodge.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Conflict requires divergence of intent and a structure that rewards continuation of that divergence.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        On our world, alignment prevents such friction from becoming culture.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        To observe your species is to observe incompatible wills becoming history.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What do you mean conflict isn't usually found between lifeforms?|War Between Lifeforms]]
            [[Did you find any parallels between your kind and mine?|War Parallels]]
            [[War is a normal part of life.|War Normal]]
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: War No Difference [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3800,525","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warNoDifference">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        There are similarities at a technical level.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Both species preserve continuity. Both respond to danger. Both form structures larger than the individual.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But nothing we have documented on our world follows your pattern.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Which pattern?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        The ability to turn opposition into identity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You do not only survive conflict.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You remember it, name yourselves through it, teach it, inherit it, and sometimes miss it when it ends.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That's a charming way of saying humans are sentimental about terrible things.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        The voice uses humor when recognition becomes uncomfortable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: War Normal [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3600,625","size":"100,100"}
<<set $compliance += 1>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warNormal">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Normalisation is a defence mechanism.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It allows the organism to remain functional inside conditions it cannot resolve.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Or maybe it means we know how the world works.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Perhaps.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        But your statement contains adaptation and surrender in the same structure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You identify destruction, accept its recurrence, then protect yourself by calling it normal.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 119.5 — 1.2 — 45.1
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That felt important. Annoyingly judgmental, but important.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Yeah, I guess some people do feel shame for their nature and wish to be more than just defined by it.|War Shame]]
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: War Parallels [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3800,425","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warParallels">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Yes, but most are misleading.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your sociability often functions as negotiation.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A method for estimating another mind before it harms you, abandons you, uses you, helps you, or joins you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        So we're just too independent for you? That sounds like a fancy way of saying you're a hive mind.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        BIOCHIP DISTORTION — SIGNAL: 119.5 — 1.2 — 45.1
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        The analogy is approximate.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We share orientation, not consciousness.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        We do not experience conflicting wants at the same time in the way humans do.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your mind can desire safety and danger, isolation and contact, truth and comfort, obedience and refusal.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        That internal division may be the root of your social complexity.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Or its wound.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: War Shame [nobr agent cartographer archive] {"position":"3800,625","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "warShame">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        Shame is a secondary pattern.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The organism observes itself, compares itself to an imagined better structure, and suffers from the distance between them.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That is not wrong.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        It is also not useless.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A species that feels shame may be capable of alteration.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A species that feels only pride may repeat itself until extinction.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Careful. That almost sounded like a compliment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
        It was a possibility.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Cart Signal Check]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>


:: StoryScript [script]
(() => {
	"use strict";

	$(document).on(":passageinit", () => {
		CTP.Logs.forEach((_, id) => {
			if (!CTP.Repository.get(id)?.persist) CTP.Logs.delete(id);
		});
		CTP.Repository.forEach(({ persist }, id) => {
			if (!persist) CTP.Repository.delete(id);
		});
	});

	var CTP = class _CTP {
		constructor(id, persist = false) {
			this.stack = [];
			this.clears = [];
			this.options = {};
			if (!id?.trim()) throw new Error(`No ID specified!`);
			this.id = id;
			this.persist = persist;
			_CTP.Repository.set(id, this);
		}
		static get Repository() {
			if (!setup["@CTP/Repository"]) setup["@CTP/Repository"] = new Map();
			return setup["@CTP/Repository"];
		}
		static get Logs() {
			if (!variables()["@CTP/Logs"]) variables()["@CTP/Logs"] = new Map();
			return variables()["@CTP/Logs"];
		}
		get log() {
			if (!_CTP.Logs.get(this.id)) _CTP.Logs.set(this.id, { lastClear: -1, index: -1, seen: -1 });
			return _CTP.Logs.get(this.id);
		}
		static getCTP(id) {
			return _CTP.Repository.get(id);
		}
		add(content, options = {}) {
			if (options.clear) this.clears.push(this.stack.length);
			this.stack.push({
				options,
				content,
				index: this.stack.length,
				element: $()
			});
			return this;
		}
		print(index) {
			const { content, options: iOpts } = this.stack[index];
			const options = {
				...this.options,
				...iOpts
			};
			const element = $(document.createElement(options.element || "span")).addClass("--macro-ctp-hidden").attr({
				"data-macro-ctp-id": this.id,
				"data-macro-ctp-index": index
			}).on("update-internal.macro-ctp", (event, firstTime) => {
				if ($(event.target).is(element)) {
					if (index === this.log.index) {
						if (firstTime) {
							if (typeof content === "string") element.wiki(content);
							else element.append(content);
							element.addClass(options.transition ? "--macro-ctp-t8n" : "");
						}
						element.removeClass("--macro-ctp-hidden");
					} else {
						if (index < this.log.seen) element.removeClass("--macro-ctp-t8n");
						element.toggleClass("--macro-ctp-hidden", index > this.log.index || index < this.log.lastClear);
					}
				}
			});
			this.stack[index].element = element;
			return element;
		}

		output() {
			const wrapper = document.createDocumentFragment();
			for (let i = 0; i < this.stack.length; i++) {
				this.print(i).appendTo(wrapper);
			}
			return wrapper;
		}

		advance() {
			if (this.log.index < this.stack.length - 1) {
				this.log.index++;
				const firstTime = this.log.index > this.log.seen;
				this.log.seen = Math.max(this.log.seen, this.log.index);
				this.log.lastClear = this.clears.slice().reverse().find((el) => el <= this.log.index) ?? -1;
				$(document).trigger("update.macro-ctp", ["advance", this.id, this.log.index]);
				this.stack.forEach(({ element }) => element.trigger("update-internal.macro-ctp", [firstTime, "advance", this.id, this.log.index]));
			}
			return this;
		}

		back() {
			if (this.log.index > 0) {
				this.log.index--;
				this.log.lastClear = this.clears.slice().reverse().find((el) => el <= this.log.index) ?? -1;
				$(document).trigger("update.macro-ctp", ["back", this.id, this.log.index]);
				this.stack.forEach(({ element }) => element.trigger("update-internal.macro-ctp", [false, "back", this.id, this.log.index]));
			}
			return this;
		}
	};
	window.CTP = CTP;

	Macro.add("ctp", {
		tags: ["ctpNext"],
		handler() {
			const id = this.args[0];
			const persist = this.args.slice(1).includes("persist");
			const ctp = new CTP(id, persist);
			const _passage = passage();
			this.payload.forEach(({ args, name, contents }) => {
				const options = {};
				if (args.includes("clear")) options.clear = true;
				if (args.includesAny("t8n", "transition")) options.transition = true;
				const elementArg = args.find((el) => el.startsWith("element:")) ?? "";
				if (elementArg) options.element = elementArg.replace("element:", "");
				if (name === "ctp") ctp.options = { ...options };
				ctp.add(contents, options);
			});
			$(this.output).append(ctp.output());
			
			if (_passage === passage()) {
				const i = Math.max(ctp.log.index, 0);
				ctp.log.index = -1;
				ctp.log.seen = -1;
				while (ctp.log.index < i) ctp.advance();
			}
		}
	});

	Macro.add("ctpAdvance", {
		handler() {
			const id = this.args[0];
			if (id) {
				const ctp = CTP.getCTP(id);
				if (ctp) ctp.advance();
				else throw new Error(`No CTP with ID '${id}' found!`);
			} else throw new Error(`No ID specified!`);
		}
	});

	Macro.add("ctpBack", {
		handler() {
			const id = this.args[0];
			if (id) {
				const ctp = CTP.getCTP(id);
				if (ctp) ctp.back();
				else throw new Error(`No CTP with ID '${id}' found!`);
			} else throw new Error(`No ID specified!`);
		}
	});
})();

/*Click za next dialog*/
$("#story").on("click", function (event) {
	if (event.originalEvent !== undefined) {
		var ignore = ["<a ", "<button ", "<input "], i, n = 0;
		for (i = 0; i < ignore.length; i++) {
			if (event.target && event.target.outerHTML && event.target.outerHTML.indexOf(ignore[i]) === 0) {
				n++
			}
		}
		if (n === 0) {
            var ctpAdvanced = false;
            
            var $ctpElement = $("[data-macro-ctp-id]").first();
            if ($ctpElement.length) {
                var id = $ctpElement.attr("data-macro-ctp-id");
                
                if (window.CTP) {
                    var ctpInstance = window.CTP.getCTP(id);
                    
                    if (ctpInstance && ctpInstance.log.index < ctpInstance.stack.length - 1) {
                        ctpInstance.advance();
                        ctpAdvanced = true;
                    }
                }
            }
            // Progress further if only one choice
			if (!ctpAdvanced && $("#passages a").length === 1) {
				$("#passages a").click();
			}
		}
	}
});


//Agent stuff


var currentVideoStart = 0;
var currentVideoEnd   = 0;
var currentVideoPart  = "";
var agentVideoActive  = false;

function ensureAgentVideoListener() {
    var bgVideo = document.getElementById('bgVideo');
    if (!bgVideo || bgVideo._hasAgentListener) return;
    bgVideo._hasAgentListener = true;

    bgVideo.addEventListener('timeupdate', function () {
        if (!agentVideoActive || currentVideoEnd <= 0) return;

        if (bgVideo.currentTime >= currentVideoEnd) {
            if (currentVideoPart === "tisina") {
                bgVideo.currentTime = currentVideoStart;
                bgVideo.play();
            } else {
                bgVideo.pause();
                agentVideoActive = false;
                currentVideoEnd  = 0;
                var iframe = document.getElementById('agent-iframe');
                if (iframe && iframe.contentWindow) {
                    iframe.contentWindow.postMessage({ action: 'video_part_ended' }, '*');
                }
            }
        }
    });
}

// Iframe
$(document).ready(function() {
    var agentContainer = $('<div id="agent-container"></div>').css({
        'position':  'fixed',
        'bottom':    '320px',
        'left':      '50%',
        'transform': 'translateX(-50%)',
        'width':     '770px',
        'height':    '150px',
        'z-index':   '1000'
    });

    var iframeHtml = '<iframe id="agent-iframe" src="" width="100%" height="100%" frameborder="0" allow="microphone" allowtransparency="true" style="background: transparent; border: none;"></iframe>';
    agentContainer.append(iframeHtml);
    $('body').append(agentContainer);
});


$(window).on('message', function (event) {
    var data = event.originalEvent.data;

    // Hide iframe
    if (data && data.action === 'hide_iframe') {
        $('#agent-container').css('display', 'none');
    }

    // Passage change
    if (data && data.action === 'advance_passage') {
        if (Story.has(data.targetPassage)) {
            Engine.play(data.targetPassage);
        } else {
            console.error('[Agent] Unknown passage: ' + data.targetPassage);
        }
    }

    // Video segment
    if (data && data.action === 'play_video_part') {
        var bgVideo = document.getElementById('bgVideo');
        if (!bgVideo) {
            window.setBackgroundVideo('Hallway_Exception.mp4');
            bgVideo = document.getElementById('bgVideo');
        }
        if (!bgVideo) return;  

        ensureAgentVideoListener();

        bgVideo.loop = false;
        agentVideoActive  = true;
        currentVideoStart = data.start;
        currentVideoEnd   = data.end;
        currentVideoPart  = data.part;

        var doSeekAndPlay = function () {
            bgVideo.currentTime = data.start;
            bgVideo.play().catch(function (e) {
                console.warn('[agentVideo] play() blocked:', e);
            });
        };

        if (bgVideo.readyState >= 2) {  
            doSeekAndPlay();
        } else {
            bgVideo.addEventListener('canplay', function onReady() {
                bgVideo.removeEventListener('canplay', onReady);
                doSeekAndPlay();
            });
            if (!bgVideo.src || bgVideo.src === window.location.href) {
                window.setBackgroundVideo('Hallway_Exception.mp4');
            }
        }
    }
});

$(document).on(':passageend', function (ev) {
    var f = document.getElementById('agent-iframe');
    if (f && f.contentWindow) {
        f.contentWindow.postMessage({ action: 'passage_changed', passage: ev.passage.title }, '*');
    }
});

window.playAgentVideo = function(partName, startTime, endTime) {
    var bgVideo = document.getElementById('bgVideo');
    if (bgVideo) {
        var iframe = document.getElementById('agent-iframe');
        if (iframe && iframe.contentWindow) {
             iframe.contentWindow.postMessage({ action: 'stop_mic' }, '*');
        }

        currentVideoStart = startTime;
        currentVideoEnd = endTime;
        currentVideoPart = partName;
        
        bgVideo.currentTime = startTime;
        bgVideo.play();
    }
};

:: StoryStylesheet [stylesheet]
.--macro-ctp-hidden {
	display: none;
}

.--macro-ctp-t8n {
	animation: macro-ctp-t8n 400ms ease-in;
}

@keyframes macro-ctp-t8n {
	from { opacity: 0; }
	to { opacity: 1; }
}

/*For click to progress*/
#story {
    min-height: 100vh;
    margin: 0; 
    padding-bottom: 50px;
}
#passages {
    padding: 2.5em 0;
}

/* =========================================================
   BACKGROUND SYSTEM — THRESHOLD
   Slike idu u: src/static/media/
   Tagovi u Twineu određuju koja se slika prikazuje.
   ========================================================= */

body {
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-color: #000;
}

#bgVideo {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center center;
    z-index: -10;
    background: #000;
}

/* ---------- INTRO / FIRST ROOM ---------- */

